{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031513-2e-fan-pygmalian-society","id":1031513,"title":"[2e Fan] Pygmalian Society","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-14T02:49:55-08:00","id":1031513,"title":"[2e Fan] Pygmalian Society","content":"<span style=\"color:Blue\">Obviously the Attainments are not finished yet but I thought I would get others opinions as I work on this project.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Franklin Gothic Medium\">Pygmalian Society</span></span></b><br /> The Sculptors affect change in the world around them and seek to awaken all the sleepers of the world. (for detail see <i>Legacies of the Sublime, page 63</i>).<br /> <br /> <b>History:</b> (for detail see <i>Legacies of the Sublime, page 65</i>).<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Franklin Gothic Medium\">Society and Culture</span></span></b><br /> The first principles of the Pygmalian Society grew out of Western occult traditions. Although most Pygmalian\u2019s don\u2019t dress up their magic in the formal principles of Rosicrucian practice any more, (for detail see <i>Legacies of the Sublime, page 66</i>).<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Franklin Gothic Medium\">Origins</span></span></b><br /> <b>Parent Path or Order:</b> Acanthus, Free Council (for detail see <i>Legacies of the Sublime, page 64</i>).<br /> <br /> <b>Nickname:</b> Sculptors<br /> <br /> <b>Background:</b> (for detail see <i>Legacies of the Sublime, page 65</i>).<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> (for detail see <i>Legacies of the Sublime, page 64</i>).<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Franklin Gothic Medium\">Doctrine</span></span></b><br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 2, Mind 2, Expression 2 and one of the following at 2 or more Empathy, Occult, Persuasion.<br /> <br /> <b>Initiation:</b> Varies and informal (for detail see <i>Legacies of the Sublime, page 65</i>).<br /> <br /> <b>Organization:</b> No formal Organization (for detail see <i>Legacies of the Sublime, page 65</i>).<br /> <br /> <b>Theory:</b> Art, in all forms, carries with it the emotions and the energies of its creator. This intense emotion can be overwhelming at times and can be used to control those that witness the art being performed.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Franklin Gothic Medium\">Magic</span></span></b><br /> <b>Ruling Arcanum:</b> Mind<br /> <br /> <b>Yantras:</b> Instrument/tool of your Art (Dedicated Magic Tool and a +1 Legacy Tool); Perform your Art in a place significant to your Art (+1 Environmental); Materials of your Art, i.e. Sheet Music, canvas, etc. (+1 Persona); Mudra (+Performance)<br /> <br /> <b>Oblations:</b> Meditate in a place significant to your Art; View another\u2019s work relevant to your Art; Create a piece of work for someone else, showing it to them, and then destroying it; Spontaneous performance of your Art; Audience at the end of a scene where you performed/displayed your Art.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Franklin Gothic Medium\">Attainments</span></span></b><br /> The attainments of the Pygmalian Society deal mainly with the manipulation of emotions, thoughts and memories. The attainments are never used instantly and take a scene to enact (with the exception of some of the optional Time effects). (for detail see <i>Legacies of the Sublime, page 69</i>).<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment:</b> Read the Audience (Initiate)<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Initiation (Gnosis 2, Mind 2 (Primary), Fate 1 (Conjunctional), Expression 2)<br /> The Initiate learns to scan his audience for emotions and this is used mainly to enhance that emotion. It is easier to amplify something that is already there then to create it from scratch. This attainment enables the initiate the use of the Mental Scan spell but only for reading the emotions of the subject. This takes a scene to cast and uses Advanced Scale.<br /> <b>Conjunctional:</b> If the initiate also has fate he can use it in conjunction with the read emotions and see Interconnections of his subject. This also takes a scene to cast and uses the Advanced Scale.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Time 1<br /> Alternatively the initiate with the time Arcanum can enact Perfect Timing as the spell. This attainment is cast instantly.<br /> <br /> <b>Second Attainment:</b> World in a Grain of Sand (Apprentice)<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 2, Mind 2, Expression 2<br /> Emotional Urging.<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Time 2<br /> Choose the Thread<br /> <br /> <b>Third Attainment:</b> Arrows of Desire (Disciple)<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 4, Mind 3<br /> Memory Hole<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Time 3<br /> Shifting Sands<br /> <br /> <b>Fourth Attainment:</b> Eternity in an Hour (Adept)<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 6, Mind 4<br /> Read the Depths<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Time 4<br /> Prophecy<br /> <br /> <b>Fifth Attainment:</b> Connections (Master)<br /> <b>Prerequisites:</b> Gnosis 8, Mind 5<br /> Social Networking<br /> <b>Optional Arcanum:</b> Time 5<br /> Temporal Pocket","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12802,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","user":"Hardwire99","date":". 01-14-2017, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T03:52:57-08:00","id":1031524,"title":"","content":"The described Conjunctional effect is actually a Combined effect and would be gated off till Gnosis 3 and it also breaks legacy attainment rules. Technically, a Pygmalian that attempted to use it would go Mad.<br /> <br /> Would you mind doing the rationale for the attainments?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T04:33:24-08:00","id":1031535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031513-2e-fan-pygmalian-society?p=1031524#post1031524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The described Conjunctional effect is actually a Combined effect and would be gated off till Gnosis 3 and it also breaks legacy attainment rules. Technically, a Pygmalian that attempted to use it would go Mad.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is straight from the Legacies of the Sublime, I moved it to the first one as I thought it would go better with that one. How would using it make them go mad and why is it not legal? Since the attainments in the 2e go off at gnosis 2, 2, 4, 6, 8 was I suppose to hold off on it until Attainment level 3. Why does it need to go off at gnosis 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031513-2e-fan-pygmalian-society?p=1031524#post1031524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you mind doing the rationale for the attainments?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically as I said the attainments deal with the manipulation of emotions, thoughts and memories. I tried to stay within that theme. I took the attainments from the Pygmalian Society from the Legacies of the Sublime and placed them as best I could, not knowing the spells that they mentioned I tried to match up descriptions. I took the old Attainment level 1 and placed it at Attainment level 2 (with the exception of leaving the conjunctional effect at level 1), I took the old Attainment level 2 and placed it at Attainment level 3 and took the old Attainment level 3 and placed it at Attainment level 4, then tried to come up with Attainment level 1 and Attainment level 5.<br /> <br /> The thought behind Attainment level was to get to know their audience to better manipulate them and that is why the Innterconnection was put at Attainment level 1, The thought behind Attainment level 5 was that by that time they are almost irresistible and that will open social doors that they didn't have until now.<br /> <br /> I always have trouble picking the appropriate Optional Arcanum spell. The Optional Arcanum spell for Attainment levels 3 and 4 are straight from the book for the Pygmalians. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T06:49:45-08:00","id":1031561,"title":"","content":"Bit of Left-Hand Path trivia twisting your legacy attainments is one way to go Mad. Since this is an attainment set up that doesn't follow 2e guidelines I'd assume it's a twisting of your attainment and thus would drive the Mage using it Mad.<br /> <br /> Why isn't it legal? Because, you have the one spell effect of Mental Scan, and you have attached the second spell effect of Interconnections to it, clearly this isn't a conjunctional effect but two spell effects combined. It could work if Fate was the Optional arcana, but it's not, so it breaks with 2e's attainment guidelines. Since it's basically a combined spell turned into an attainment and you can't cast combined spells until Gnosis 3 this combined effect shouldn't be possible until Gnosis 3.<br /> <br /> This is one case of following the 1e legacy guidelines too accurately not being a great idea.<br /> <br /> Why do you have Temporal Pocket in there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T07:06:26-08:00","id":1031564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031513-2e-fan-pygmalian-society?p=1031561#post1031561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bit of Left-Hand Path trivia twisting your legacy attainments is one way to go Mad. Since this is an attainment set up that doesn't follow 2e guidelines I'd assume it's a twisting of your attainment and thus would drive the Mage using it Mad.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am assuming the the not following 2e guidelines is the combination spell part. that is easy take out the Interconnection, I only had it there because it was in the 1e write-up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031513-2e-fan-pygmalian-society?p=1031561#post1031561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why isn't it legal? Because, you have the one spell effect of Mental Scan, and you have attached the second spell effect of Interconnections to it, clearly this isn't a conjunctional effect but two spell effects combined. It could work if Fate was the Optional arcana, but it's not, so it breaks with 2e's attainment guidelines. Since it's basically a combined spell turned into an attainment and you can't cast combined spells until Gnosis 3 this combined effect shouldn't be possible until Gnosis 3.<br /> <br /> This is one case of following the 1e legacy guidelines too accurately not being a great idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said I can remove it all together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031513-2e-fan-pygmalian-society?p=1031561#post1031561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you have Temporal Pocket in there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Conceptual, I have heard time after time of people loosing track of time just wasting the day away listening to music, looking at pictures, reading a book. The rest of the world just seems to not exist and time goes much faster. &quot;You look us and didn't even realize that it was midnight already.&quot; That type of concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T07:13:30-08:00","id":1031567,"title":"","content":"That sounds more like Temporal Stutter to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T07:32:15-08:00","id":1031573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1031513-2e-fan-pygmalian-society?p=1031567#post1031567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds more like Temporal Stutter to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ya that could work also and is conceptually sound. I will consider it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}